    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0351" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2764</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-30">November 30,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of November 21, 1918, together with its enclosure,
                    regarding the wish of your Government to be appropriately represented at the
                    coming conferences, especially those dealing with topics in which Switzerland
                    has interests of a general or private character.</p>
                <p>In reply, I beg to inform you that this Government has received with sympathy the
                    request of the Swiss Government and it is not in a position to give a final
                    reply until after arrival of the President in Paris.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
